You want to add a link for each post on your website, so that users can share or access individual posts.

To achieve this, you'll need to make a few changes to your Nginx configuration file. Here's a suggested modification:

**1. Create a new location block for post links**

Add the following block to your main `server` block:
```nginx
location ~ ^/(.*)$ {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    internal;
}
```
This block matches any URL path (e.g., `/post/1`, `/post/2`, etc.).

**2. Add a rewrite rule to generate post links**

Insert the following rewrite rule below the `location /` block:
```nginx
rewrite ^(/.*)$ /post/$1 permanent;
```
This rule redirects any URL path to `/post/<path>` (e.g., `/post/1` becomes `/post/1`).

**3. Update the `index.html` fallback**

Modify the `location /` block to:
```nginx
location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    rewrite ^(.*)$ /post/$1 permanent;
}
```
This ensures that the rewrite rule is applied only when no specific file or directory is found.

**4. Add a post link to each post**

In your `index.html` or `post.html` templates, add a link to each post:
```html
<a href="/post/{{ post.id }}">Read more</a>
```
Replace `{{ post.id }}` with the actual post ID or a unique identifier of your choice.

**5. Update your existing `location /api` block (optional)**

If you have a backend API handling post requests, you may want to update the `location /api` block to include the post ID in the request:
```nginx
location /api {
    proxy_pass https://askfundu.com:5000/post/$arg_post_id;
    # ... (rest of your proxy configuration)
}
```
This allows your backend API to receive and process requests for specific posts.

After making these changes, reload your Nginx configuration:
```
sudo nginx -s reload
```
Verify that the changes took effect by accessing your website and checking if the post links are generated correctly.

Remember to update your templates accordingly, and adjust the rewrite rules if you need to handle additional scenarios (e.g., post revisions, categories, tags).<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

